13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
is a 2003 American action crime thriller film based on the
1975–76 television series of the same name.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The film was directed by Clark Johnson from a screenplay by David Ayer and
David McKenna, based on a story by Ron Mita and Jim McClain.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
It stars Samuel L.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Jackson, Colin Farrell, Michelle Rodriguez, LL Cool J, Josh Charles,
Jeremy Renner, Brian Van Holt and Olivier Martinez with Reg E.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Cathey and Larry Poindexter in supporting roles.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Like the TV series, the film revolves around a police Special Weapons and
Tactics (SWAT) team operating in Los Angeles California.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The plot follows Hondo (Jackson) and his SWAT team as they are tasked to escort an imprisoned drug kingpin/international
fugitive to prison after he offers a $100 million reward to anyone who can break him out of police custody.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Plans for a film adaptation of the 1975 TV series began in the
1990s, but never materialized until the early 2000s.

21
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
Johnson was hired as director and Jackson, Farrell
and LL Cool J were cast in 2002.

22
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:26,000
was released in the United States on August 8, 2003, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

23
01:39:40,000 --> 01:39:46,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $207.7 million
worldwide against a production budget of $70 million.

24
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
A direct-to-video sequel, S.W.A.T.: Firefight, was released in 2011.

25
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:26,000
The film explores themes of liberation, transport of
prisoners, special unit, los angeles, california.

26
01:52:40,000 --> 01:52:46,000
The tone is intense.
